{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgubztA6sGNvaQoDnXjVa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`. I haven't run it or checked it against a Camel 4.22 runtime.\n\n```yaml\n- route:\n    id: nightly-order-export\n    from:\n      uri: quartz:orders/nightlyExport\n      parameters:\n        cron: \"0 0 2 * * ?\"\n        trigger.timeZone: Europe/Berlin\n      steps:\n        - log:\n            message: Nightly order export started\n        - to:\n            uri: direct:export\n```\n\n- **`quartz:orders/nightlyExport`**: the Quartz endpoint, written as `groupName/timerName`. The group is `orders` and the timer is `nightlyExport`.\n- **`cron: \"0 0 2 * * ?\"`**: a Quartz cron expression (seconds, minutes, hours, day-of-month, month, day-of-week) that fires at 02:00:00 every day. In YAML `parameters` you can use plain spaces; the `+` encoding is only needed when the cron goes inside a URI string.\n- **`trigger.timeZone: Europe/Berlin`**: makes the schedule follow Berlin time, including the switch between CET and CEST. Without it, the server's default time zone is used. It's passed through the Quartz component's `trigger.` prefix options.\n- **`log`, then `to: direct:export`**: logs \"Nightly order export started\" and then calls the export route.\n\nYou'll need a route that consumes from `direct:export` in the same Camel context, or the call will fail at runtime."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":4514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":740},"output_tokens":502,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7139ec55-58ed-480f-b1e5-18c6a88e9c5f","uuid":"dbf3bd41-f